---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="Accessibility Statement | Diaz Tech Home Page" current="">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Accessibility Statement</h1>
      <p style="color:var(--color-muted); font-size:14px;">Last updated: September 21, 2026</p>

      <p>
        Diaz Technologies Inc. is committed to making www.diaztech.net usable for as many
        visitors as possible, including people with disabilities. This page describes what
        we've actually done toward that, and what's still outstanding. We'd rather this be
        accurate than aspirational.
      </p>

      <h2>What's in place</h2>
      <ul style="padding-left:18px;">
        <li>Page content is structured with a logical, sequential heading order</li>
        <li>Images have descriptive alternative text</li>
        <li>Navigation, including the mobile menu, is fully operable by keyboard alone</li>
        <li>Clickable elements are sized and spaced to standard touch-target guidelines</li>
        <li>Form fields are labeled for screen reader compatibility</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What this site doesn't need to worry about</h2>
      <p>
        This is a static, content-focused site. We don't publish audio or video, so
        requirements like captioning, transcripts, and audio descriptions don't apply here.
      </p>

      <h2>What's still outstanding</h2>
      <p>
        We haven't completed a full manual accessibility audit — this page reflects targeted
        fixes plus automated testing, not a comprehensive screen-reader pass or a tool like axe
        or WAVE. Known open items:
      </p>
      <ul style="padding-left:18px;">
        <li>Color contrast hasn't been verified against every part of the homepage's gradient background</li>
        <li>There's no "skip to main content" link for keyboard users yet</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Requests, issues, and suggestions</h2>
      <p>
        If you find an accessibility issue on the site, or need assistance, you're welcome to
        contact us through the organization's accessibility coordinator:
      </p>
      <p>
        Aliya Moxey<br />
        734-999-8453<br />
        <a href="mailto:ar.moxey@diaztech.net">ar.moxey@diaztech.net</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
